QUIZ

Let’s check your knowledge about the concepts you just learned.

1. Which of the following did you add your data set as in IBM Watson Studio?

    -> Artifact

    -> Asset ✅

    -> Resource

    -> Project
    
    💡In IBM Watson Studio, your data set is considered an asset. To add a data set, you select
    the Asset tab and then add your data file. The data set is then displayed on the Asset tab.


2. After you provisioned the database (Cloud Object Storage) what did you select to access
    AI/Machine Learning?

    -> Code Engine

    -> Cloud Foundry

    -> Resource list

    -> Catalog ✅

    💡To provision AI/Machine Learning, you selected Catalog from the top menu.


3. Which of the following services did you provision first for your project?

    -> Two competing resource names

    -> AI / Machine Learning

    -> Database storage ✅

    -> All assets

    💡Once you’ve logged in and selected Catalog in the Dashboard, it’s a best practice to create
    your database storage first, this allows you to set up your AI model without having to stop and
    provision the storage for your data.


4. When you selected the CSV file in All assets, what did you see?

    -> A list of possible storage locations

    -> A preview of the data to used when training your model ✅

    -> A proposed name for your project

    -> A set of provision options for Watson Machine Learning

    💡A CSV file is a set of comma-delineated data. When you select the CSV file in the All assets
    tab, the Preview asset tab displays showing the data you can use to train your model.


5. After you finished setting up your IBM Watson Studio service, which of the following did you do
    next?

    -> Created a new project ✅

    -> Set up the holdout and split

    -> Downloaded historic data about loan defaults

    -> Created a set of algorithms

    💡After you set up your IBM Watson Studio service, you created a new project.